#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#In this example, "Engine Mount" is selected in the advanced settings. Therefore, the engine (and any rigid parts which move together with the engine, e.g. transmission, clutch/torque converter) is treated as one independent rigid body from the chassis (sprung mass).
#
#Engine body location and how the engine is mounted are specified on other screen: Engine Mounts: Engine Mass and Geometry.
#
#The sprung mass (kg) on this screen is supposed to be the entire sprung mass including the engine body which is specified on the other screen. The VehicleSim solver automatically subtracts the engine mass from the entire sprung mass in order to not duplicate the engine mass.
#
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

